Subject: [PATCH 03/15] replication: leader-gate background work

Intent: JELLYFIN_ROLE unset or 'leader' behaves exactly like stock; any
other value disarms scheduled-task triggers, trigger-originated scans,
and LiveTV/DVR timer arming, with one startup log line stating the role
and what is disarmed. Manual API-invoked runs work on any pod. Carried
unchanged onto 12.x: ScheduledTaskWorker, TaskManager, RecordingsHost
and TimerManager are identical to 10.11.11, and 12.x adds no hosted
service and no background timer (its one new timer, SyncPlay's group
wait timer, is request-driven).
Ceiling: only arming is gated. A run that is asked for (task execution
through the API, QueueLibraryScan after a library edit or wizard
completion) executes on whichever pod receives the request, and that
pod then starts its realtime library monitor.
Drop when: upstream ships first-class multi-instance roles.

Patch: 0004
